<title>UK: British input prices rise 0.5 pct in October.</title>
<headline>British input prices rise 0.5 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British producer input prices rose 0.5 percent in October, fuelled by a sharp rise in oil prices, official figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>But input prices fell 2.0 percent on a year-on-year-basis. Output prices rose 0,2 percent in October for a 2.3 percent year-on-year rise. Crude oil prices rose 6.8 percent in October over September and 44.3 percent on a year-on-year basis.</p>
</text>
